-edged, diffused, and slowly traveling; there are no abrupt specular spikes, no strobing, no flashing, no glittering, and no rapid brightness jumps anywhere on the ring. Polished gold reads as warm satin luster rather than mirror reflection. The gold alexandrite vine ring shown in <Picture 1> rests on a surface of deep black velvet, replacing the original background entirely. The velvet has a soft, dense nap with gentle natural folds that absorb light, creating pools of pure negative space around the piece. The camera begins an extremely slow push in with small amplitude at slow speed, as if emerging from darkness toward the ring. A single broad, diffused side light enters from the right and slowly washes across the ring — first along the gold vine band with a soft warm satin glow, then across the pear-shaped alexandrite. The stone awakens gradually from near-darkness as color bleeds slowly from within its facets, shifting from deep raspberry purple at the crown toward teal-blue at the pavilion in a continuous, smooth gradient. The black velvet absorbs all stray light, leaving only the ring itself with a quiet, even luminescence. A single soft-edged shadow stretches leftward from the band.\n\n[Shot 2] At 00:05.000, the camera cuts to an extreme macro close-up of the alexandrite's table facet, the stone occupying the center of the 16:9 frame with the gold vine prongs softly blurred at the edges. The background is pure velvety black. The camera performs a slow arc shot with small amplitude at slow speed, orbiting just a few degrees around the gem. The broad diffused light source gradually shifts from warm to cool in color temperature, and the alexandrite responds with a slow internal color change: the upper half deepens into velvety purplish-red while the lower half transforms into teal-blue, the two tones bleeding into each other across the girdle with no hard edges. A soft diffuse sheen passes slowly across the surface of one small diamond on the lower vine — a gentle brightening and dimming rather than a sparkle or flash. No facet strobes, no pinprick flashes, no scintillation effects appear on any stone. The gem glows as if lit from behind its facets, with smooth, gradated internal light rather than surface glitter.\n\n[Shot 3] At 00:10.000, the shot transitions to a low-angle side profile of the ring, resting on a gentle fold of black velvet that cradles the band. The camera pulls out with small amplitude at slow speed, gradually revealing the full three-dimensional vine construction: the intertwining double gold bands, the sculpted leaf reliefs curling around the gallery, and the vine stems rising to cradle the pear-shaped stone. Warm diffused side light rakes along the gold curves with soft-gradated highlights — each leaf and stem emerges from darkness with a satin warmth, never a sharp mirror glint. As the camera continues its slow retreat, the light narrows progressively and smoothly: first the outer leaves dim gradually, then the band fades slowly, until only the pear-cut alexandrite remains lit with a soft inner glow, a single quietly luminous teardrop suspended in the blackness. The stone's light dissolves smoothly into darkness as the video ends, with no abrupt cutoff.\n\noverall_soundscape: Near-total silence, with only the faintest room tone beneath. At the opening, the soft nap of black velvet makes an almost imperceptible rustle as the light passes over it. A barely audible low metallic resonance hums beneath the color shift, so quiet it feels like vibration rather than sound. No chimes, no pings, no percussive sounds enter — the silence is as smooth and continuous as the light.\n\nnon_diegetic_music: A single sustained low cello drone opens the piece at near-whisper volume, joined every several seconds by one sparse piano note at a very slow tempo with long decay and heavy pedal sustain. The piano notes cluster slightly during the color-change close-up, then thin to silence as the light narrows in the final shot, leaving only the cello drone dissolving smoothly into nothing.\n\n\n"], "inputs": [{"widget": {"name": "value"}, "name": "value", "label": "value", "type": "STRING", "localized_name": "值"}], "flags": {}, "type": "PrimitiveStringMultiline", "mode": 0, "bgcolor": "#353", "size": [762.294189453125, 599.58447265625], "pos": [46.54731750488281, 5561.85791015625], "id": 232, "properties": {"widget_ue_connectable": {}, "Node name for S&R": "PrimitiveStringMultiline"}, "order": 18}, {"outputs": [{"name": "positive", "links": [345, 433], "label": "positive", "type": "CONDITIONING", "localized_name": "positive"}, {"name": "LATENT", "links": [440], "label": "LATENT", "type": "LATENT", "localized_name": "Latent"}], "color": "#223", "widgets_values": ["", 1344, 768, 124, "max"], "inputs": [{"name": "clip", "link": 272, "label": "clip", "type": "CLIP", "localized_name": "clip"}, {"shape": 7, "name": "vae", "link": 420, "label": "vae", "type": "VAE", "localized_name": "vae"}, {"shape": 7, "name": "audio_vae", "link": 368, "label": "audio_vae", "type": "VAE", "localized_name": "audio_vae"}, {"shape": 7, "name": "ref_images.ref_image_0", "link": 455, "label": "ref_images.ref_image_0", "type": "IMAGE", "localized_name": "ref_image_0"}, {"shape": 7, "name": "ref_images.ref_image_1", "link": 456, "label": "ref_images.ref_image_1", "type": "IMAGE", "localized_name": "ref_image_1"}, {"shape": 7, "name": "ref_images.ref_image_2", "link": 457, "label": "ref_images.ref_image_2", "type": "IMAGE", "localized_name": "ref_image_2"}, {"shape": 7, "name": "ref_images.ref_image_3", "link": 465, "label": "ref_images.ref_image_3", "type": "IMAGE", "localized_name": "ref_image_3"}, {"shape": 7, "name": "ref_images.ref_image_4", "link": 466, "label": "ref_images.ref_image_4", "type": "IMAGE", "localized_name": "ref_image_4"}, {"shape": 7, "name": "ref_images.ref_image_5", "link": 467, "label": "ref_images.ref_image_5", "type": "IMAGE", "localized_name": "ref_image_5"}, {"shape": 7, "name": "ref_ima